# Accounting Journal Entry
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Accounting — a header-detail document, debit=credit, prepared and posted by different people
# Case 9 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: accounting-chart-of-account.menata, accounting-journal-entry-line.menata, accounting-fiscal-period.menata
#
# Note: the individual debit/credit facts belong to Journal Entry Line, a separate
# Object that references back to this one (- Journal Entry : Journal Entry, see
# accounting-journal-entry-line.menata) — no "Lines" field is declared here. This is
# the ordinary Object References pattern (001-object.md §Relationships): "a Journal
# Entry has many Lines" is already implied by "each Line references one Journal
# Entry," with no separate grammar needed for the collection side. Events and
# Constraints below still refer to "Lines" in plain business language (Journal Entry
# Line records scoped to this Journal Entry), the same way accounting-fiscal-
# period.menata refers to "Every Journal Entry in this Fiscal Period" without a
# declared field. (An earlier revision of this file modeled Lines as a provisional
# `Table of (...)` field, believing no Language grammar existed for this yet — see
# roadmap.md's dated correction note for why that was a misdiagnosis.)

Journal Entry

Fields

- Entry Number : Text
- Entry Date : Date
- Fiscal Period : Fiscal Period
- Memo : Rich Text
- Status : Draft | Posted
- Prepared By : User
- Posted By : User
- Posting Date : Date

Events

When Post

    Posting Date Today

    Posted By Current User

    Sum of Lines Debit Amount must equal sum of Lines Credit Amount

    Fiscal Period must not be Closed

    Posted By must not equal Prepared By

    Status Posted

Constraints

- Entry Number is required.
- Entry Date is required.
- Fiscal Period is required.
- At least one Journal Entry Line is required.

    Sum of Lines Debit Amount must equal sum of Lines Credit Amount.

    Fiscal Period must not be Closed.

    Posted By must not equal Prepared By.

Permissions

Accountant

- Post

Supervisor

- Post

Views

- Entry Form : Form
- Draft Entries : List
- Posted Entries : List
- Entry Detail : Detail
